./docs/plans/2026-04-21-sso-user-identity-linkage/design.md:130078:- **Provider-scoped identity-link table**. GitLab `identities` and Gitea `ExternalLoginUser` both persist a provider discriminator, an external identifier, and a local `user_id` in a separate structure. This is the most direct fit when one local user may be linked to multiple IdPs.
./docs/plans/2026-04-21-sso-user-identity-linkage/design.md:130082:Keycloak's `FEDERATED_IDENTITY` falls in the separate-table family as well, but introduces an additional realm scope and stores broker-specific metadata because Keycloak is itself an identity broker rather than an application with a local username model.
./docs/plans/2026-04-21-sso-user-identity-linkage/design.md:130086:- Separate tables add one extra lookup during sign-in compared with `GetUser(Username)`, but they avoid coupling authentication subjects to user-facing usernames.
